From: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] sched_ext: Specialize the DSQ hashtable compare

Local backport of the September 21, 2026 authored patch to CachyOS
7.2.8.
The signature is joined as in the maintainer acceptance reply.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260921171928.1639407-1-usama.arif@linux.dev/
Link: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/09/21/2444
Accepted for sched_ext/for-7.4; see:
Link: https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/09/21/2516

Compare the known u64 DSQ key directly instead of using a generic
runtime-length memcmp.
This local backport has build and VM coverage; hardware latency is
unmeasured.
No new local Signed-off-by is asserted.
---
diff --git a/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c b/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
--- a/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/ext/ext.c
@@ -163,10 +163,20 @@
  */
 static DEFINE_PER_CPU(struct task_struct *, direct_dispatch_task);
 
+static __always_inline int dsq_cmpfn(struct rhashtable_compare_arg *arg, const void *ptr)
+{
+	const struct scx_dispatch_q *dsq = ptr;
+
+	BUILD_BUG_ON(sizeof_field(struct scx_dispatch_q, id) != sizeof(u64));
+
+	return dsq->id != *(const u64 *)arg->key;
+}
+
 static const struct rhashtable_params dsq_hash_params = {
 	.key_len		= sizeof_field(struct scx_dispatch_q, id),
 	.key_offset		= offsetof(struct scx_dispatch_q, id),
 	.head_offset		= offsetof(struct scx_dispatch_q, hash_node),
+	.obj_cmpfn		= dsq_cmpfn,
 };
 
 static LLIST_HEAD(dsqs_to_free);
